hange</td><td>-57,589</td><td>-57,589</td></tr><tr><td>Adjustment for change in valuation of SDR holdings and allocations<sup>1</sup></td><td>17,609</td><td>17,609</td></tr><tr><td>Interest (+) or net charges (-) on:</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>SDRs</td><td>48,266</td><td>48,266</td></tr><tr><td>U.S. Government securities</td><td>177,476</td><td>177,476</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign exchange</td><td>88,296</td><td>88,296</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>Income from operations</b></td><td>274,058</td><td>274,058</td></tr><tr><td><b>Net income (+) or loss (-)</b></td><td>274,058</td><td>274,058</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1042, 796, 1120], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"1 Beginning July 1974, the International Monetary Fund adopted a technique for valuing the SDRs based on a weighted average of exchange rates for the currencies of selected member countries. The U.S. SDR holdings and allocations are valued on this basis beginning July 1974.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [842, 1040, 1492, 1127], \"page_id\": 116}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Annual balance sheets for fiscal 1934 through 1940 appeared in the 1940 \\\"Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury\\\" and those for succeeding years appeared in subsequent reports through 1980. Quarterly balance sheets beginning with December 31, 1938, have been published in the \\\"Treasury Bulletin.\\\" Data from inception to September 30, 1978, may be found on the statements published in the January 1979 \\\"Treasury Bulletin.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [353, 87, 1284, 111], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"FINANCIAL REPORT OF THE UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT, EXCERPT\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1446, 82, 1490, 108], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"119\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [195, 193, 1423, 231], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Financial Report of the United States Government\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 264, 803, 436], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The following pages are excerpted from the 2000 \\\"Financial Re-port of the United States Government.\\\" The report and accompanying information, prepared and published annually by the Financial Management Service, are modeled after corporate-type reports and are developed on an accrual basis of accounting.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 436, 801, 519], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The excerpts represent some of the most noteworthy information contained in the Financial Report. Data for the Financial Report are compiled from Federal program agency ac-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 556, 770, 622], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Statement of Operations and Changes in Net Position\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 634, 805, 858], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"This Statement reports the results of Government operations. This includes revenues principally generated by the Government's sovereign power to tax, levy duties, and assess fines and penalties. This Statement covers the cost of Government operations, net of revenue earned from the sale of goods and services to the public. It also includes any adjustments and unrecorded transactions that affect the net position.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 870, 250, 893], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Revenue\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 898, 807, 1009], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"\\\"In di vidual Income Tax and Tax With hold ings\\\" cons ist of Federal in di vidual in come taxes, So cial Se curity taxes, Medicare taxes, and rail road re tire ment taxes, net of re lated re-funds.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1011, 811, 1261], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"\\u201cMiscellaneous Earned Revenues\\u201d consists of earned revenues received from the public with virtually no associated cost. This category includes revenues generated by the Federal Communications Commission from the sale of spectrum licenses to promote open-air communication services to the public (spectrum auctions). It also includes rents and royalties on the Outer Continental Shelf Lands resulting from the leasing and development of mineral resources on public lands.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1270, 565, 1296], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Net Cost of Government Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1299, 801, 1381], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The State ment of Net Cost sum ma rizes the \\\"Net Cost of Government Operations,\\\" which is gross cost less earned revenue.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1393, 454, 1421], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Unreconciled Transactions\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1428, 805, 1534], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"\\u201cUnrec onciled Trans actions\\u201d are adjustments needed to net position due to unrec onciled and unac counted for differences in the process of consolidating all the agencies\\u2019 financial statements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1549, 528, 1575], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Net Position, Beginning of Period\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1579, 805, 1666], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The \\u201cNet Position, Beginning of Period\\u201d reflects the net position reported on the prior year\\u2019s Balance Sheet as of the end of that fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1674, 446, 1700], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Prior Period Adjustments\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1704, 805, 1784], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"\\\"Prior Period Adjustments\\\" are revisions to adjust the beginning net position. Refer to Note 17\\u2014Prior Period Adjustments for detailed information.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1801, 459, 1824], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Net Position, End of Period\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1829, 807, 1890], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"This amount reflects the net position as of the end of the fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 266, 1492, 405], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"counting systems Governmentwide. Treasury also presents a management discussion and analysis, the customary notes to the financial statements, a section on \\\"Stewardship Information\\\" and supplemental information, in the complete document.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 408, 1494, 519], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The General Accounting Office (GAO) is required by law to audit the Financial Report. GAO\\u2019s report, as well as the complete Financial Report, can be easily accessed through the internet at www.fms.treas.gov/cfs.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 561, 1169, 592], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Statement of Net Cost\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 606, 1488, 691], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"This State ment pres ents the net cost of fis cal 2000 Gov ern-ment op er a tions. It also shows the cost to carry out na tional priorities as de ter mined by law.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 691, 1494, 969], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"It cate go rizes costs by ma jor func tion. It pres ents costs in much the same way as does the bud get, ex cept that costs are al- located to func tions based on Gen erally Ac cepted Ac counting Prin ciples (GAAP). Thus, this State ment re ports costs on an ac crual ba sis and in some cases al lo cates them differ ently than the bud get. Forex am ple, this State ment al lo cates the cost of pen sions and post-retirement health ben e fits among all the func tions that em ploy work ers. The bud get cate go rizes pen- sion pay ments to ci vil ian re tirees, mil i tary re tirees and bene fi- cia ries as a subfunc tion un der \\u201cIn come se cu rity.\\u201d\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 969, 1494, 1138], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The budget categoryizes agency contributionstoretirement funds as intragovernmental outlays distributed among all the functions that employ workers. A description of each of the functions and the components of net cost for the activities included in each function is presented in Supplemental Information as \\u201cNet cost detail.\\u201d\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 25, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [827, 1141, 1490, 1188], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"This Statement contains the following three components for each function:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 26, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [847, 1190, 1333, 1223], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The gross cost of Government operations.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 27, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [847, 1226, 1477, 1275], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The revenues earned from the sale of goods and provision of services to the public.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 28, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [845, 1280, 1479, 1304], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The net cost of Government operations, which is gross\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 29, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [845, 1306, 1122, 1332], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"cost less revenue earned.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 30, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1339, 962, 1370], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Gross Cost\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 31, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 1372, 1494, 1454], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"\\\"Gross Cost\\\" in cludes the full cost of all func tions. These costs may be di rectly traced, as signed on a cause-and-effect basis, or reason ably allo cated to the function.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 32, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1464, 1018, 1487], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Earned Revenue\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 33, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1490, 1492, 1546], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"This is revenue the Government earned by providing goods and services to the public at a price.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 34, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 1556, 931, 1582], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Net Cost\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 35, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1584, 1488, 1638], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The \\u201cNet Cost\\u201d of Government operations is computed by subtracting \\u201cEarned Revenue\\u201d from \\u201cGross Cost.\\u201d\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 36, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1659, 1051, 1685], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"Balance Sheet\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 37, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1704, 1490, 1900], \"page_id\": 117}], \"content\": \"The Balance Sheet shows the Government\\u2019s assets and liabilities. When combined with Stewardship Information, this information presents a more comprehensive understanding of the Government\\u2019s financial position. All of the line items on the Balance Sheet are described in the Notes to the Financial Statements. For example, the first note provides information on the accounting policies for assets and liabilities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 38, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 82, 182, 106], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"120\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [352, 82, 1277, 108], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"FINANCIAL REPORT OF THE UNITED STATES GOVERNMENT, EXCERPT\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 207, 548, 238], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"United States Government\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 238, 965, 269], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"Statement of Operations and Changes in Net Position\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 271, 743, 304], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"for the Year Ended September 30, 2000\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 339, 342, 365], \"page_id\": 118}], \"content\": \"(In billions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 403, 262, 429], \"page_id\": 118}],