Federal Reserve Bank of New York. Estimates reflect the 1989 benchmark to 1994, the 1994 benchmark to September 2001, the March 2000 benchmark to September 2002, the June 2002 benchmark to December 2003, the June 2003 benchmark to March 2004, the June 2004 benchmark to March 2005, and the June 2005 benchmark to February 2006. 9 Includes individuals, Government-sponsored enterprises, brokers and dealers, bank personal trusts and estates, corporate and non-corporate businesses, and other investors.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1381, 2046, 1497, 2081], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"June 2006\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 97, 175, 125], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"50\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [537, 212, 1093, 250], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Market Yields\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 269, 798, 363], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"The table in this section presents yields on Treasury marketable securities for maturities ranging from 1 month to 30 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 365, 800, 799], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"Table MY-1 lists Treasury market bid yields at constant maturities for bills, notes, and bonds. These Constant Maturity Treasury rates (CMTs) are interpolated from the Treasury yield curve and published daily at Treasury's Domestic Finance web site, www.ustreas.gov/offices/domestic-finance/debt-management/interest-rate/yield.shtml. The yield curve is fitted daily using a hermite cubic spline. For inputs, Treasury primarily uses the bid yields of the on-the-run securities (most recently auctioned Treasury securities in all maturity tranches that Treasury currently auctions) as quoted in the secondary bond market as of approximately 3:30 p.m. each trading day. CMT yields are based on semiannual interest payments and are read at constant maturity points to develop a consistent data series.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 266, 1490, 422], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"The quotations used by Treasury to calculate the bid yields and fit the yield curve are obtained by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. The Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System also publishes the Treasury constant maturity data series in its weekly Statistical Release H.15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 429, 1492, 710], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"On July 31, 2001, Treasury expanded its constant maturity index to include a 1-month constant maturity yield. On February 18, 2002, Treasury discontinued the 30-year constant maturity yield and replaced it in the MY-1 with a 20-year maturity yield. Historical data for the 20-year maturity is available from the Board of Governors' Statistical Release H.15. On February 9, 2006, Treasury reintroduced the 30-year yield and is now publishing both the 20- and 30-year constant maturity rates.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 714, 1490, 834], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"Prior to January 2003, this section also included data on long-term Treasury, corporate and municipal yields (Table MY-2 and Chart MY-B). Effective January 2003, Table MY-2 and Chart MY-B were discontinued.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [330, 903, 1284, 978], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"TABLE MY-1.\\u2014Treasury Market Bid Yields at Constant Maturities: Bills, Notes, and Bonds*\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [432, 990, 1184, 1016], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"[In percentages. Source