Note 3)</td><td>32.3</td></tr><tr><td>Loans receivable (Note 4)</td><td>207.6</td></tr><tr><td>Taxes receivable (Note 5)</td><td>23.3</td></tr><tr><td>Inventories and related property (Note 6)</td><td>185.2</td></tr><tr><td>Property, plant, and equipment (Note 7)</td><td>298.5</td></tr><tr><td>Other assets (Note 8)</td><td>59.7</td></tr><tr><td>Total assets</td><td>911.5</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1035, 279, 1063], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"Liabilities:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [166, 1098, 1455, 1843], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Accounts payable (Note 9)</td><td>91.0</td></tr><tr><td>Federal debt securities held by the public (Note 10)</td><td>3,408.5</td></tr><tr><td>Federal employee and veteran benefits payable (Note 11)</td><td>2,757.8</td></tr><tr><td>Environmental and disposal liabilities (Note 12)</td><td>301.2</td></tr><tr><td>Benefits due and payable (Note 13)</td><td>77.8</td></tr><tr><td>Loan guarantee liabilities (Note 4)</td><td>37.3</td></tr><tr><td>Other liabilities (Note 14)</td><td>175.0</td></tr><tr><td>Total liabilities</td><td>6,848.6</td></tr><tr><td>Commitments and contingencies (Note 18)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Net Position</td><td>(5,937.1)</td></tr><tr><td>Total liabilities and net position</td><td>911.5</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [168, 1890, 1240, 1919], \"page_id\": 120}], \"content\": \"The accompanying notes in the complete document are an integral part of these financial statements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1443, 94, 1490, 127], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"123\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [388, 193, 1240, 238], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Airport and Airway Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 290, 794, 514], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"The Air port and Air way Trust Fund was es tab lished on the books of Trea sury in fis cal 1971, ac cord ing to pro vi sion of the Air port and Air way Rev e nue Act of 1970 [49 United States Code 1742(a), repealed]. The Tax Equity and Fiscal Re spon si bility Act of 1982 (Pub lic Law 97-248, dated Sep- tem ber 3, 1982) re es tab lished the trust fund in the In ter nal Revenue Code (26 United States Code 9502) effective Sep- tem ber 1, 1982.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 512, 792, 712], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"Trea sury trans fers from the gen eral fund to the trust fund amounts equiv a lent to the taxes re ceived from trans por ta tion of persons and prop erty by air, gas o line and jet fuel used in commercial and non commercial aircraft, and an in ter na tional de par ture tax. The Om ni bus Bud get Rec on cil i a tion Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-508, dated November 5, 1990) in - creased rates for the ex cise taxes trans ferred to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 712, 792, 792], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"Trea sury bases these trans fers on es ti mates made by the Secretary of the Trea sury. These are subject to ad just ments in later trans fers in the amount of ac tual tax re ceipts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 794, 792, 879], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"The Tax payers Re lief Act of 1997 (Pub lic Law 105-34), ef fec tive Oc to ber 1, 1997, ex tended the avi at ion ex cise taxes for 10 years. The Act in cluded other pro vi sions that:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 879, 792, 1016], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"\\u2022 Re-tained the ex ist ing freight way bill and gen eral avi ation fuel/gas taxes. It also re-tained a spe cial rule applied to flights be tween the con ti nen tal United States and Alaska or Hawaii. The $6 de parture tax is in dexed to the Consumer Price Index. Effective fiscal year 2001, the tax is $6.40.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1016, 794, 1162], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"Con verted the 10 per cent ad va lo rem tax on do mes tic pas sen ger tick ets to a com bi na tion of ad va lo rem/flight seg- ment tax over 3 years, be gin ning Oc to ber 1, 1997. Be gin ning Oc to ber 1999 through Sep tem ber 30, 2007, the tax is 7.5 per- cent, plus in 2001, a $2.75 tax per seg ment.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 285, 1492, 429], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"Imposed a new 7.5 per cent tax on payments to airlines for frequent flyer and similar awards by banks and credit card companies, merchants and frequent flyer program partners, such as other airlines, hotels or rental car companies, and other businesses.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 429, 1488, 542], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"In creased the cur rent $6 in ter na tional de par ture tax to $12 per pas sen ger and added a $12 in ter na tional ar rival tax, in dexed to the Con sumer Price In dex. Ef fec tive 2001, the tax is $12.80.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 542, 1488, 601], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"Lowered tax rates on flights to cer tain ru ral air ports to 7.5 percent with out a flight seg ment com po nent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 601, 1484, 681], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"Transferred revenues from the 4.3 cents-per-gallon aviation fuel tax dedicated to reducing the national deficit from the general fund to the Airport and Airway Trust Fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 681, 1492, 879], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"When the provisions of 26 United States Code 9602(b) are met, amounts available in the fund exceed outlay requirements, Treasury invests excess amounts in public debt securities and cred its the interest to the fund. Additional sums from the general fund also are credited as authorized and made available, by law, if they are needed to meet outlay requirements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 879, 1494, 1072], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"Treasury makes available to the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), Department of Transportation (DOT), amounts required for outlays to carry out the Airport and Airway program. The Secretary of the Treasury makes other charges to the trust fund to transfer certain refunds of taxes and certain outlays, under section 34 of the Internal Revenue Code (IRC).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1072, 1488, 1245], \"page_id\": 121}], \"content\": \"An nual re ports to Con gress, re quired by 26 U.S.C. 9602 (a), are sub mit ted by the Sec re tary of the Trea sury, af ter con sultation with the Sec re tary of Trans por tion. These re ports are re quired to cover the fi nan cial con di tion and re sults of op er a tions of the fund dur ing the past fis cal year and those ex pected dur ing the next 5 fis cal years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 94, 184, 120], \"page_id\": 122}], \"content\": \"124\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [716, 92, 907, 125], \"page_id\": 122}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [470, 193, 1155, 262], \"page_id\": 122}], \"cont